From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:43:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] runtime: wrap-aware tracking phase lock (pacing_lock_on =
 "tracking", 0035b)

0035 steered by a plain median of raw sample ages. The age is a phase on [0, period): off the setpoint the
median sat mid-period, the integral wound up, the trim pinned at -5000 ppm and slewed the phase ~5.5 ms/s,
faster than one step per 90 frames (10-26, gated: lock err +8-9 ms, trim -5000, sample age 8-11 ms).

TrackingPhaseLock (header-only, pure) wraps each sample's error to +/-P/2 around pacing_lock_age_ms,
averages a step's errors on the circle, resets the integral on a wrap, steps every 15 frames and caps
the trim at 1500 ppm. Ages over 1.5 periods (lost tracking packets) are skipped. The pacing log line
gains wraps=N.

tests/TestTrackingPhaseLock.cpp simulates 24 sessions per case (start phase across the period, clock
offset -500/0/+500 ppm, arrival jitter 0.5/1.5/3.5 ms, age reaching the lock 2 frames late): every
session's median age lands at 3.05-3.60 ms, spread <= 0.16 ms, trim pinned <= 1 %. The sim also says
the wrap is the fix: 0035's step and cap with the wrapped error hold too. Not yet run on the stand.

